{"cuisine/fusion-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/fusion-cuisine","n":"Fusion cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]],"sub":"Diaspora cuisine in United States of America","intro":[["Fusion cuisine is a cuisine that combines elements of different culinary traditions that originate from different countries, regions, or cultures. Cuisines of this type are not categorized according to any one particular cuisine style and have played a part in many contemporary restaurant cuisines since the 1970s."],["The term fusion cuisine, added to the Oxford English Dictionary in 2002, is defined as \"a style of cookery which blends ingredients and methods of preparation from different countries, regions, or ethnic groups; food cooked in this style.\""]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"fusion-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fusion_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Dishes","count":6,"links":[["Blok's Restaurant","dish/blok-s-restaurant"],["Karen Keygnaert","dish/karen-keygnaert"],["Kojacha","dish/kojacha"],["Saucebox","dish/saucebox"],["The Peak Lookout","dish/the-peak-lookout"],["Variety Jones (restaurant)","dish/variety-jones-restaurant"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Fusion cooking","count":16,"links":[["American Jewish cuisine","cuisine/american-jewish-cuisine"],["Cajun cuisine","cuisine/cajun-cuisine"],["Chinese American cuisine","cuisine/chinese-american-cuisine"],["Cuisine of the Pennsylvania Dutch","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-pennsylvania-dutch"],["Filipino-American cuisine","cuisine/filipino-american-cuisine"],["Floribbean cuisine","cuisine/floribbean-cuisine"],["German-American cuisine","cuisine/german-americans-cuisine"],["Greek-American cuisine","cuisine/greek-american-cuisine"],["Indian-American cuisine","cuisine/indian-american-cuisine"],["Italian-American cuisine","cuisine/italian-american-cuisine"],["Japanese-American cuisine","cuisine/japanese-american-cuisine"],["Korean-American cuisine","cuisine/korean-americans-cuisine"],["Mexican-American cuisine","cuisine/mexican-american-cuisine"],["New American cuisine","cuisine/new-american-cuisine"],["Thai-American cuisine","cuisine/thai-american-cuisine"],["Vietnamese-American cuisine","cuisine/vietnamese-americans-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/0e/Minchi_e_bacalhaus.jpg/500px-Minchi_e_bacalhaus.jpg","w":500,"h":374,"by":"K.Y.K.Z.K.","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minchi_e_bacalhaus.jpg"}},"cuisine/chettinad-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/chettinad-cuisine","n":"Chettinad cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Tamil cuisine","cuisine/tamil-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in India","intro":[["Chettinadu cuisine is the cuisine of a community called the Nagarathars, from the  Chettinad region in Sivaganga district of Tamil Nadu state in"],["India. Chettinad cuisine is perhaps the most renowned fare in the Tamil Nadu repertoire. It uses a variety of spices and the dishes are made with fresh ground masalas. Chettiars also use a variety of sun-dried meats and salted vegetables, reflecting the dry environment of the region. Most of the dishes are eaten with rice and rice based accompaniments such as  dosas, appams, idiyappams, adais and idlis. The Chettiars, through their mercantile contacts with Burma, learnt to prepare a type of rice pudding made with sticky red rice. The chefs of Manapatti village near Singampunari are experts in cooking Chettinad cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"chettinad-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chettinad_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Archana's Kitchen (Oriya)","ref":"site/archanaskitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"archanaskitchen.com","note":"Chettinad-tagged recipes on Archana Doshi's large Indian recipe site.","url":"https://www.archanaskitchen.com/tag/chettinad-recipes/page-2","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"The Bangala Table: Flavors and Recipes from Chettinad","ref":"cookbook/the-bangala-table-flavors-and-recipes-from-chettinad","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Sumeet Nair and Meenakshi Meyyappan","note":"Chettinad recipes from The Bangala heritage hotel in Karaikudi.","url":"","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Tamil cuisine","cuisine/tamil-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/c6/ChickenChettinad.JPG/500px-ChickenChettinad.JPG","w":500,"h":749,"by":"Maccess Corporation","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.5","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ChickenChettinad.JPG"}},"dish/berowra-waters-inn":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/berowra-waters-inn","n":"Berowra Waters Inn","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Berowra Waters Inn is a restaurant, owned and run by Head Chef Brian Geraghty, located at Berowra Waters along Berowra Creek (a tributary of the Hawkesbury River), near Ku-ring-gai Chase National Park, 50 minutes from downtown Sydney, Australia. It is unique due to its being accessed only by private ferry or airplane, as well as being one of Pritzker Prize-winning Australian architect Glenn Murcutt's only venues regularly open to the public. For many years Berowra Waters Inn represented the cutting edge of both Australian design and cuisine. The menu changed frequently but was a 'mix of classic French and Modern Australian'."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-berowra-waters-inn"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berowra_Waters_Inn"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","ref":"site/pardonyourfrench-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","ref":"site/lacuisinedegeraldine-fr","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","ref":"site/newcaledonia-travel","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an earth oven.","url":"https://www.newcaledonia.travel/nz/gastronomy-wine/gastronomy/kanak-cooking","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from French cuisine","links":[["'t Fornuis","dish/t-fornuis"],["'t Misverstant","dish/t-misverstant"],["'t Vlasbloemeken","dish/t-vlasbloemeken"],["&moshik","dish/moshik"],["Aan de Poel","dish/aan-de-poel"],["Adrian (restaurant)","dish/adrian-restaurant"],["Adventureland Bazaar","dish/adventureland-bazaar"],["Alain Ducasse at The Dorchester","dish/alain-ducasse-at-the-dorchester"],["Albufera sauce","dish/albufera-sauce"],["Alex (restaurant)","dish/alex-restaurant"],["Andouillette","dish/andouillette"],["Arpège (restaurant)","dish/arpege-restaurant"],["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Atelier Crenn","dish/atelier-crenn"],["Au Coin des Bons Enfants","dish/au-coin-des-bons-enfants"],["Au Crocodile","dish/au-crocodile"],["Au Pied de Cochon (Mexico City)","dish/au-pied-de-cochon-mexico-city"],["Auberge (restaurant)","dish/auberge-restaurant"],["Auberge De Kieviet","dish/au