nresa-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manresa_(restaurant)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["California cuisine","cuisine/california-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from California cuisine","links":[["Campanile (restaurant)","dish/campanile-restaurant"],["Cheese Board Collective","dish/cheese-board-collective"],["Chez Panisse","dish/chez-panisse"],["Commander's Palace","dish/commander-s-palace"],["Disney's Grand Californian Hotel & Spa","dish/disney-s-grand-californian-hotel-spa"],["Hula's Island Grill","dish/hula-s-island-grill"],["Madrona Manor","dish/madrona-manor"],["Michael's (restaurant)","dish/michael-s-restaurant"],["Napa Rose","dish/napa-rose"],["Quince (restaurant)","dish/quince-restaurant"],["Rich Table","dish/rich-table"],["Spago","dish/spago"],["Stars (restaurant)","dish/stars-restaurant"],["Sushi bake","dish/sushi-bake"],["The Mountain House","dish/the-mountain-house"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/58/Manresa_%28restaurant%29.jpg/500px-Manresa_%28restaurant%29.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"LittleT889","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manresa_(restaurant).jpg"}},"dish/rice-and-beans":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/rice-and-beans","n":"Rice and beans","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Latin American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Rice and beans, or beans and rice, is a category of dishes from many cultures around the world where the staple foods of rice and beans are combined in some manner. The grain and legume combination provides several important nutrients and many calories, and both foods are widely available. The beans are usually seasoned, while the rice may be plain or seasoned. If the beans do not top the rice, the two components may be mixed together, separated on the plate, or served separately."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-rice-and-beans"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rice_and_beans"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Latin American cuisine","cuisine/latin-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Beans","ingredient/beans"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]},{"h":"More from Latin American cuisine","links":[["Bollo","dish/bollo"],["Buñuelo","dish/bunuelo"],["Cardenas (supermarket)","dish/cardenas-supermarket"],["El Cielo (restaurant)","dish/el-cielo-restaurant"],["Frijoles negros","dish/frijoles-negros"],["La Michoacana Meat Market","dish/la-michoacana-meat-market"],["Mi Pueblo Food Center","dish/mi-pueblo-food-center"],["Quince cheese","dish/quince-cheese"],["Tamale","dish/tamale"],["Vallarta Supermarkets","dish/vallarta-supermarkets"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/ca/Rice_and_Beans.jpg/500px-Rice_and_Beans.jpg","w":500,"h":224,"by":"Lorena Galicia","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rice_and_Beans.jpg"}},"dish/saheena":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/saheena","n":"Saheena","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Trinidad and Tobago cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Saheena (also spelled sahina or sahiena, ) is a street food and snack in the cuisine of Trinidad and Tobago."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-saheena"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saheena"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Trinidad and Tobago cuisine","cuisine/trinidad-and-tobago-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Spinach","ingredient/spinach"],["Split pea","ingredient/split-pea"],["Taro","ingredient/taro"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Cooking with Ria","ref":"site/cookingwithria-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cookingwithria.com","note":"Trinidadian home recipes from Ria Mathura.","url":"https://cookingwithria.com/about","suggested":true},{"name":"Trini Gourmet","ref":"site/trinigourmet-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"trinigourmet.com","note":"Long-running Trinidad and Tobago food blog with local recipes.","url":"https://trinigourmet.com/","suggested":true}]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/19/FOOD_Saheena_1.jpg/500px-FOOD_Saheena_1.jpg","w":500,"h":650,"by":"Grueslayer","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FOOD_Saheena_1.jpg"}},"dish/the-hoito":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/the-hoito","n":"The Hoito","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Finnish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["The Hoito Restaurant (often referred to as “The Hoito” by locals) is a Finnish-Canadian restaurant in Thunder Bay, Ontario, Canada established in 1918 and housed in the bottom floor of the historic Finnish Labour Temple.  The Hoito operated continuously on 314 Bay Street, in the historic Bay & Algoma neighbourhood, for more than a century until closing due to the COVID-19 pandemic in March 2020. It was one of the oldest co-operatively owned and operated restaurants in Canada. It had been anticipated that the restaurant would reopen in early summer 2022. However, during the early evening hours of December 22, 2021, amid on-going renovations, smoke could be seen billowing from the rooftop, and The Hoito restaurant suffered extensive damage when a massive fire burned through the Finnish Labour Temple building above. The building is now gone, with new construction underway."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-the-hoito"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hoito"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Finnish cuisine","cuisine/finnish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Finnish cuisine","links":[["Blodpalt","dish/blodpalt"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Egg butter","dish/egg-butter"],["Glögg","dish/glogg"],["Joulutorttu","dish/joulutorttu"],["Kalakukko","dish/kalakukko"],["Karelian hot pot","dish/karelian-hot-pot"],["Kesäkeitto","dish/kesakeitto"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Kuivaliha","dish/kuivaliha"],["Lanttulaatikko","dish/lanttulaatikko"],["Lohikeitto","dish/lohikeitto"],["Lörtsy","dish/lortsy"],["Semla","dish/semla"],["Smörgåstårta","dish/smorgastarta"],["Strong beer","dish/strong-beer"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/50/The_Hoito_restaurant_in_Thunder_Bay%2C_Ontario..jpg/500px-The_Hoito_restaurant_in_Thunder_Bay%2C_Ontario..jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"Abuabyad","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Hoito_restaurant_in_Thunder_Bay%2C_Ontario..jpg"}},"dish/the-ledbury":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/the-ledbury","n":"The Ledbury","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from British cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["The Ledbury is a restaurant located on Ledbury Road, Notting Hill, London, England. It held two Michelin stars from 2010 until 2021, when it lost them as it shut due to Covid-19 restrictions being impractical for the restaurant, making it ineligible for assessment by Michelin inspectors. It has also been featured in S.Pellegrino World's 50 Best Restaurants. The restaurant reopened in February 2022, after being closed for almost 2 years. It regained both Michelin stars in the 2023 Michelin Guide and was promoted to three Michelin stars in the 2024 Michelin guide."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-the-ledbury"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ledbury"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Great British Chefs: traditional British recipes","ref":"site/greatbritishchefs-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"greatbritishchefs.com","note":"UK chef-driven recipe site with a large section of classic British dishes.","url":"https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/features/our-most-popular-traditional-british-recipes","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from British cuisine","links":[["68–86 Bar and Restaurant","dish/68-86-bar-and-restaurant"],["Banbury cake","dish/banbury-cake"],["Battenberg cake","dish/battenberg-cake"],["Black pudding","dish/black-pudding"],["Bread sauce","dish/bread-sauce"],["Carpetbag steak","dish/carpetbag-steak"],["Chelsea bun","dish/chelsea-bun"],["Christmas pudding","dish/christmas-pudding"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Crumble","dish/crumble"],["Crumpet","dish/crumpet"],["Curry in the United Kingdom","dish/curry-in-the-united-kingdom"],["Digestive biscuit","dish/digestive-biscuit"],["Dinner by Heston Blumenthal","dish/dinner-by-heston-blumenthal"],["Dundee cake","dish/dundee-cake"],["English muffin","dish/english-muffin"],["Flies' graveyard","dish/flies-graveyard"],["Flummery","dish/flummery"],["Fritter","dish/fritter"],["Garibaldi biscuit","dish/garibaldi-biscuit"],["Gidleigh Park","dish/gidleigh-park"],["Hot cross bun","dish/hot-cross-bun"],["Hovis biscuit","dish/hovis-biscuit"],["Jammie Dodgers","dish/jammie-dodgers"],["Melba toast","dish/melba-toast"],["Mince pie","dish/mince-pie"],["Phall","dish/phall"],["Pickled egg","dish/pickled-egg"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Ploughman's lunch","dish/ploughman-s-lunch"],["Potted shrimps","dish/potted-shrimps"],["Prawn cocktail, steak and Black Forest gateau","dish/prawn-cocktail-steak-and-black-forest-gateau"],["Restaurant Andrew Fairlie","dish/restaurant-andrew-fairlie"],["Restaurant James Sommerin","dish/restaurant-james-sommerin"],["Rhodes Twenty Four","dish/rhodes-twenty-four"],["Rich tea","dish/rich-tea"],["Rose & Crown Pub & Dining Room","dish/rose-crown-pub-dining-room"],["Sausage roll","dish/sausage-roll"],["Scotch egg","dish/scotch-egg"],["Shepherd's pie","dish/shepherd-s-pie"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b4/Ledbury%2C_Notting_Hill%2C_W11_%285499132198%29.jpg/500px-Ledbury%2C_Notting_Hill%2C_W11_%285499132198%29.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Ewan Munro from London, UK","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ledbury%2C_Notting_Hill%2C_W11_(5499132198).jpg"}},"dish/wahe":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/wahe","n":"Wähe","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Swiss cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Wähe (which derives from the dialect in the regions of Basel, Zurich, Baden and Alsace) is a baked dish typical of Swiss and Alemannic (German) cuisine. A wähe consists of a casing (typically made of shortcrust pastry, but sometimes yeast dough or puff pastry) and a topping of a custard enveloping either fruit, vegetables or cheese. The custard and fruits or vegetables are baked together. The preparation is thus very similar to that of the French quiche or tarte."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-wahe"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/W%C3%A4he"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Swiss cuisine","cuisine/swiss-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Custard","ingredient/custard"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Helvetic Kitchen","ref":"site/helvetickitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"helvetickitchen.com","note":"Andie Pilot's blog of Swiss home cooking and baking, with notes on Swiss cookbooks.","url":"https://www.helvetickitchen.com/recipes/retrospective","suggested":true},{"name":"Cuisine Helvetica","ref":"site/cuisinehelvetica-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cuisinehelvetica.com","note":"Heddi Nieuwsma's Swiss recipes and food culture from her life in Switzerland.","url":"https://cuisinehelvetica.com/swiss-recipes","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Swiss cuisine","links":[["Älplermagronen","dish/alplermagronen"],["Basler Läckerli","dish/basler-lackerli"],["Birnbrot","dish/birnbrot"],["Bündnerfleisch","dish/bundnerfleisch"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Carac (pastry)","dish/carac-pastry"],["Cervelat","dish/cervelat"],["